# Basic checks only

After a code change, stop at basic checks. Do not launch heavier validation or other agents unless the user asked for that check in this conversation, or explicitly approved it when asked.

## Allowed without asking

- Editor diagnostics on the files just edited (lints, type errors reported by the IDE).

## Ask first, then wait

- Full or project builds and test runs: `mvn`, Gradle, `npm run build`, `npm test`, `tsc`, Spring Boot, or starting a dev server.
- Browser tools: navigate, snapshot, click, or any other in-browser validation.
- Any subagent (explore, general-purpose, Bugbot, security review, CI investigator, best-of-n, or a cloud task).

Ask in one sentence naming the command or agent and why. Do not start it in the same turn as the question.

```text
# BAD — change landed, then a full boot and a browser pass with no ask
mvn -f backend/pom.xml spring-boot:run
browser_navigate http://localhost:3000

# GOOD — edit, read lints on the touched files, then ask
Read diagnostics for BulkMigrationTab.tsx.
Ask: "Run the frontend typecheck?"
```
